      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a fairly old extension, however, I don\u0027t think we can require + enforce that all devices using graphite/Vulkan have it.\n\ngpuinfo.org shows that most Android, Windows, and Linux devices do support it (~85%). We care most about Android. Looking into devices that lack support, I think some of these would cause problems were we to enforce having this extension... mostly Samsung devices (Notes 4, 5, 7, 8; Galaxy S9+...). \n\n@michaelludwig@google.com, LMKWYT? Having your/Greg\u0027s opinion on devices we must support is helpful.\n\nLink to the list:\nhttps://vulkan.gpuinfo.org/listdevicescoverage.php?platform\u003dandroid\u0026extension\u003dVK_KHR_driver_properties\u0026option\u003dnot",
